data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Let $m = \\max_k z_k$ along the axis. Then $\\log\\sum_k e^{z_k} = m + \\log\\sum_k e^{z_k - m}$, and every\nexponent $z_k - m$ is at most $0$. Compute the result as $(z_j-m)-\\log\\sum_k e^{z_k-m}$. Keeping both terms shifted avoids losing the log normalizer to a huge common offset. Only an out-of-range negative log-probability must become $-\\infty$."},"hints_note":null}

